00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.559
John: Right!

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:04.259
So the Project for Awesome is an annual charity
event in which the Nerdfighter community tries

00:01:04.259 --> 00:01:06.890
to decrease world suck and increase world
awesome.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:11.420
Nat: Uh, the Project for Awesome will be on
December 12th and 13th, which is actually

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.540
4 days away from my birthday.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.610
4 and 5 days away from my birthday.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:15.610
When's your birthday?

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:16.610
December 17th.

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.939
That's when the Project for Awesome usually
is, but we had to move it because it's the

00:01:18.939 --> 00:01:19.939
end of the Paper Towns shoot.

00:01:19.939 --> 00:01:20.939
Cara: Because it's his birthday!!!!

00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:21.939
Nat: Yeah, it's my birthday!

00:01:21.939 --> 00:01:23.000
John: Yeah, we gotta focus on Nat's birthday
that day.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Yay!

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Nat: Yeah, project for Nat.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.780
I thought this change might be better received
if it came from, you know, Nat and Carr - oh

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:32.750
- this just got so weird.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.880
I'm having such an unpleasant experience.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.590
So we're moving the Project for Awesome to
December 12th mostly because of the Paper

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.610
Towns shoot but also because of Nat's birthday.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:42.180
I'm sorry about that, but I, I really want
to be part of it.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.680
But Hank, we also want to talk to Nerdfighteria
about maybe doing other things differently,

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.020
beginning with comments.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:51.280
So the Project for Awesome started out in
2007 with YouTubers making videos about, like,

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.979
charity, instead of, you know, cats on Roombas
or whatever.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:57.690
This is back when people discovered YouTube
videos primarily on, like, the "Most Discussed

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.060
Page" or the "Top Rated Page."

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.659
Nerdfighteria came together to essentially
hijack YouTube's algorithm.

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:06.119
And that was amazing, back when those pages
existed.

00:02:06.119 --> 00:02:11.010
But then, YouTube made comments progressively
less important to discovery.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.080
Basically, comments spamming just doesn't
work anymore.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.340
I dunno where to vlog from so I think I'll
go to this creepy abandoned building.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.730
So the other challenge that we have is that
traditionally, 100% of the Project for Awesome's

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:24.470
money goes to charities chosen by Nerdfighteria
at projectforawesome.com.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.870
So this is a great system, but two things:
first, it's hard to get, like, matching money

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.360
from wealthy private donors.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.000
And second, because we're all always so busy
comment-spamming, I think that sometimes there

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.760
isn't enough attention paid to the actual,
like, voting for charities.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.190
So here is my proposal, and Nerdfighteria,
I want your feedback about this, any new ideas

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:41.190
you might have...

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:44.210
The first day of the Project for Awesome,
we raise money for three organizations that

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:48.860
are known to be excellent and efficient when
it comes to combating global poverty and disease.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:52.370
This will allow us to get a lot of matching
donations, like potentially hundreds of thousands

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:55.310
of dollars, and also to decrease a known cause
of world suck.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:58.300
And then the second day of the Project for
Awesome will be all about raising money for

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.870
charities chosen by Nerdfighteria, and instead
of comment-spamming, we'll have, like, meaningful

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.500
discussions in comments of Project for Awesome
videos.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.690
So to summarize, Hank, here is my proposal:
December 12th and 13th instead of December

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:09.690
17th and 18th.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.370
On December 12th, at noon Eastern, everyone
who wants to uploads a video about a charity

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:14.370
of their choice.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:17.500
Members of the Nerdfighter community try to
watch as many of those videos as possible,

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:21.870
have substantive discussions in comments,
and then all of Nerdfighteria votes carefully

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.810
and thoughtfully for their favorite charities
at projectforawesome.com.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:29.810
All of the money raised after the first day
of the Project for Awesome will go to those

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:34.540
charities, all of the money raised on the
first day that are well-regarded in the field

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.970
of global health and poverty.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.660
And I can't decide if I should go in this
door.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:38.760
I kind of want to.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.890
Oh, it's a bathroom!

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.030
Oh, it's quite lovely.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:46.250
We've experimented a lot with the format and
scope of the Project for Awesome over the

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:50.230
years, but one thing has never changed: it
is my favorite time of year to be a Nerdfighter,

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.840
and I can promise you: this year, the perks
are going to be amazing.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.310
I'm going to go back to the movie set, I will
see you- this is the last time I get to say

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.150
this, it's kind of a bummer- tomorrow.

